DTSTART:20261106T133000Z
DTEND:20261106T143000Z
SUMMARY:US jobs report (October)
DESCRIPTION:October nonfarm payrolls and unemployment rate.\n\nEconomists p
 olled by LSEG expected 65k. A strong print would add to the case for a Dec
 ember Fed hike\, which is bearish for crypto and long-duration tech and su
 pportive for the dollar. Outcome: payrolls rose 165k\, well above the 65k 
 estimate.\n\nBLS Employment Situation schedule: https://www.bls.gov/schedu
 le/news_release/empsit.htm\nFox Business: US economy adds 165\,000 jobs in
  October: https://foxbusiness.com/economy/us-jobs-report-october-2026
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/empsit.htm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1ff3391996ed63bc@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261112
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:US-Ukraine-Russia talks\, Abu Dhabi
DESCRIPTION:First three-way round in about nine months\, focused on securit
 y guarantees.\n\nRussia agreed to resume the three-way talks after Witkoff
  met Putin on October 21. A ceasefire isn't on the agenda\, and Russia rej
 ects any European troops in Ukraine. Strikes on Ukraine's grid and a Russi
 an refinery came hours before the talks. Progress would weigh on oil and l
 ift European cyclicals. A collapse would support oil and gold. Outcome: th
 e talks ended on November 11 without a breakthrough\, and Witkoff and Kush
 ner said they'd fly to Moscow to meet Putin the next day.\n\nKyiv Independ
 ent: envoys to Moscow as Abu Dhabi talks end without breakthrough: https:/
 /kyivindependent.com/2nd-day-of-trilateral-peace-talks-begins-between-ukra
 ine-russia-us-in-abu-dhabi/\nNews On AIR: hostilities continue before US-b
 rokered talks: https://newsonair.gov.in/hostilities-continue-between-russi
 a-and-ukraine-before-scheduled-us-brokered-talks/\nADN: Putin agrees to re
 sume three-way talks: https://www.adn.com/nation-world/2026/10/21/putin-ag
 rees-to-resume-three-way-talks-on-ukraine-war-with-kyiv-and-washington-kre
 mlin-says/
CATEGORIES:geopolitics
URL:https://kyivindependent.com/2nd-day-of-trilateral-peace-talks-begins-be
 tween-ukraine-russia-us-in-abu-dhabi/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e9f8bb7efd634991@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART:20261110T133000Z
DTEND:20261110T143000Z
SUMMARY:US CPI (October)
DESCRIPTION:October consumer prices\, with forecasts of +0.3% headline and 
 +0.2% core month over month.\n\nSeptember headline was +0.6%. Fed Governor
  Waller said core at 0.3% or higher would call for a stronger policy move.
  A hot print lifts yields and the dollar\, which hurts crypto\, tech and g
 old. BLS isn't publishing year-over-year rates because of the 2025 shutdow
 n. Outcome: headline +0.4% and core +0.3%\, both hot. The 2Y rose 17bp to 
 4.74%\, the 10Y neared 5% and CME odds of no December move fell to about 3
 %.\n\nBLS CPI release schedule: https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/
 cpi.htm\nBenzinga: Hot CPI pushes 10-year yield to 5%: https://www.benzing
 a.com/markets/equities/26/11/63117496/stock-market-today-hot-cpi-treasury-
 yields-5-percent-nvidia-slides\nStartup Fortune: December Fed hike now pri
 ced in: https://startupfortune.com/treasury-yields-jump-after-hot-october-
 cpi-with-a-december-fed-hike-now-priced-in/
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/cpi.htm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:77daac68318d714e@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261113
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:Witkoff and Kushner meet Putin in Moscow
DESCRIPTION:US envoys take the Abu Dhabi results to Putin after the three-w
 ay talks ended without a deal.\n\nThe Abu Dhabi agenda covered a ceasefire
 \, energy and Black Sea security. Ukraine wants a European-led reassurance
  force and Article 5-style guarantees. AP reports neither side has shown w
 illingness to compromise\, and Moscow wants Europe kept out of the direct 
 talks. Movement toward a ceasefire would weigh on oil and lift European cy
 clicals. A breakdown would support oil and gold. Outcome: Witkoff and Kush
 ner met Putin for about two hours\, then briefed Zelensky in Dublin. They 
 agreed the largest prisoner exchange of the war\, but there was no ceasefi
 re\, and the Kremlin played down a seat for Europe.\n\nCNN: Witkoff and Ku
 shner meet Zelensky after talks with Putin: https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/12
 /politics/ukraine-witkoff-kushner-putin-peace-talks-intl\nKyiv Independent
 : envoys to Moscow as Abu Dhabi talks end: https://kyivindependent.com/2nd
 -day-of-trilateral-peace-talks-begins-between-ukraine-russia-us-in-abu-dha
 bi/\nKyiv Post: second day of Abu Dhabi talks ends: https://www.kyivpost.c
 om/post/89761
CATEGORIES:geopolitics
URL:https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/12/politics/ukraine-witkoff-kushner-putin-p
 eace-talks-intl
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1b2afa1d94c8076a@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART:20261117T220000Z
DTEND:20261117T230000Z
SUMMARY:Nvidia Q3 FY2027 earnings
DESCRIPTION:Nvidia reports the quarter ended October 25 after the US close.
  Consensus is about $108.8bn revenue and $2.47 EPS.\n\nThe consensus figur
 es come from MarketBeat via InsiderFinance. A miss or weak China guidance 
 would extend the semis and AI selloff and drag crypto-linked stocks. A bea
 t could spark a sharp rebound in semis and the Nasdaq. Jensen Huang resign
 ed on November 11 (8-K). CFO Colette Kress is interim CEO and keeps the CF
 O role while the board searches for a permanent CEO. Nvidia says results r
 emain on schedule for 1:20pm PT\, with the call at 2pm PT. Guidance from a
 n interim CEO is the main risk. On November 14 two major investors urged t
 he board to consider Huang's return (CNBC)\, and House Republicans want hi
 m to testify on November 18\, so leadership headlines can swamp the number
 s. Options priced a 5.4% move before the August report (ORATS via Reuters)
 . No current read found. On November 15 the FT reported Huang is weighing 
 a comeback\, and Asian chip stocks fell on November 16 ahead of the report
  (Cointelegraph). On November 16 the shares fell 4.1% and the semis ETF SM
 H 5.1% as the board reportedly ruled out a Huang return (Cointelegraph)\, 
 while Trump backed reinstating him (BBC). The US also moved to block China
 's remote access to AI chips (Al Jazeera). Outcome: Nvidia beat estimates 
 and gave a stronger sales outlook (CNBC)\, the shares rose after hours (Ma
 rketWatch) and the company said it won't reinstate Huang (BBC). Revenue an
 d guidance figures weren't found in search by November 19. The shares clos
 ed down 2.9% on November 18\, the first session after the report.\n\nNVIDI
 A 8-K: CEO transition: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001045810/
 000104581026000082/nvidiaannouncesceotransiti.htm\nNVIDIA: conference call
  for Q3 results: https://investor.nvidia.com/news/press-release-details/20
 26/NVIDIA-Sets-Conference-Call-for-Third-Quarter-Financial-Results/\nInsid
 erFinance: Nvidia earnings set for Nov. 17: https://www.insiderfinance.io/
 news/nvidia-earnings-set-for-nov-17-amid-sell-signals
CATEGORIES:stocks
URL:https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001045810/000104581026000082/n
 vidiaannouncesceotransiti.htm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7dafd152bbadda75@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261120
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:APEC summit\, Shenzhen\, possible Trump-Putin-Xi meeting
DESCRIPTION:APEC leaders meet in Shenzhen\, and the White House says Trump\
 , Putin and Xi plan a joint meeting in China.\n\nThe White House announced
  the planned three-way meeting on November 14 (BBC)\, the first ever betwe
 en the three. SCMP reports Xi and Trump are set for talks at APEC but majo
 r deliverables are expected to wait for the G20 in December\, and one anal
 yst called a trilateral possibly no more than a photo opportunity. Kremlin
  aide Ushakov says Putin will attend\, and Xi reportedly said the three wo
 uld probably meet but not to discuss Ukraine. A US-China trade framework o
 r progress on a Ukraine deal would lift the Nasdaq\, the Hang Seng and cry
 pto and weigh on oil and gold. A cancelled meeting or a public split would
  keep the risk-off tone. On November 16 CNBC reported China confirmed the 
 three-way summit\, and the NYT said the Nvidia fallout hangs over the Trum
 p-Xi talks. Trump left for the summit on November 16\, and the NYT reporte
 d an open split in his administration on China policy. The US-China trade 
 truce runs to January 10 (TNW)\, so wording on an extension matters. Befor
 e the summit both governments extended their suspensions of trade measures
  and port fees (SCMP). On November 18 Xi and Putin opened talks\, and Xi c
 alled for removing trade and investment barriers ahead of his meeting with
  Trump and Putin (CNBC). On November 19 Xi greeted Putin and Trump before 
 the three-way summit\, and Trump said he wants to talk nuclear arms with b
 oth (Al Jazeera). No communique had been reported by the morning of Novemb
 er 19. Outcome: the three-way meeting lasted 90 minutes and agreed that nu
 clear wars leave no winners\, and it did little to settle US-China trade t
 ensions (Modern Ghana). The trade truce still runs out in January.\n\nSCMP
 : Shenzhen ready to host Xi\, Trump and Putin: https://scmp.com/news/china
 /politics/article/3371206/chinas-shenzhen-ready-host-xi-trump-and-putin-du
 ring-apec-summit\nSCMP: Xi and Trump set APEC talks\, deliverables wait fo
 r G20: https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3373969/xi-and-tr
 ump-set-apec-talks-major-deliverables-expected-wait-g20\nModern Ghana: wha
 t impact will the Shenzhen summit have: https://www.modernghana.com/news/1
 546082/what-impact-will-the-shenzhen-summit-have-on-the.amp
CATEGORIES:geopolitics
URL:https://scmp.com/news/china/politics/article/3371206/chinas-shenzhen-re
 ady-host-xi-trump-and-putin-during-apec-summit
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1b82baf38329491b@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261120
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:Anthropic starts trading on Nasdaq
DESCRIPTION:Anthropic's shares are expected to begin trading under the tick
 er ANT after the largest IPO on record.\n\nCNBC reports the IPO raised ove
 r $81bn\, topping SpaceX\, and the BBC puts the valuation at up to $1.5tn.
  The deal priced on the evening of November 18 after a marketed range of $
 70 to $78 a share (XTB\, Leverage Shares). It lands with Nvidia down about
  30% in a month and the Nasdaq under its 50-day average. A strong first da
 y would help AI and tech sentiment\, and a weak one would add to the Nasda
 q selloff. A raise this large can also pull cash out of other AI names. CZ
  says a tokenized version is coming to BNB Chain on IPO day (CoinDesk). Ou
 tcome: the IPO priced at $83\, the shares opened at $111.50 and closed the
  first day at $97.17\, up 17% (CNBC). Stocks fell to session lows as tradi
 ng began\, and the S&P 500 closed in correction the next day.\n\nNasdaq Tr
 ader: data technical news\, November 11\, 2026: https://nasdaqtrader.com/T
 raderNews.aspx?id=DTN2026-28\nTechRepublic: Anthropic opens at $111.50 in 
 record Nasdaq debut: https://www.techrepublic.com/article/news-anthropic-i
 po-nasdaq-trading-debut/\nStock Titan: Anthropic IPO\, ANT first trading d
 ay: https://www.stocktitan.net/articles/anthropic-ipo-live-ant-first-tradi
 ng-day-2026
CATEGORIES:stocks
URL:https://nasdaqtrader.com/TraderNews.aspx?id=DTN2026-28
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cdbdc968934e2c24@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261124
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:Nvidia reinstates Jensen Huang as CEO
DESCRIPTION:Nvidia's board brought Huang back as CEO twelve days after his 
 resignation\, and US stocks had their best day since April 2025.\n\nThe bo
 ard had said on November 17 that it wouldn't rehire him. Trump said he con
 vinced Nvidia to reinstate Huang and drew criticism for it (BBC). The US s
 anctioned Megaspeed\, the Singapore firm at the centre of the case\, and p
 ut it on the trade blacklist the same day (NYT\, CNBC). Outcome: Nvidia cl
 osed up 31.48%\, its best day since May 2003\, and the S&P 500 rose about 
 4.7% to end a seven-session losing streak (Yahoo Finance). Bitcoin fell 1.
 6% on the day. Governance questions and the national security probe remain
  open\, so new disclosures can still hit semis. The next day Nvidia fell 5
 .9% to $155.38 and a semiconductor index lost 7.9% (Yahoo Finance\, NBC)\,
  after Attorney General Blanche declined to say whether the Justice Depart
 ment or FBI had investigated Huang. On November 25 the shares fell another
  3.9%\, and S&P warned the credit rating could be cut over management and 
 governance risk (CNBC).\n\nYahoo Finance: stocks post best day since April
  2025 as Nvidia soars 31%: https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/live/stock-ma
 rket-today-monday-november-23-dow-sp-500-nasdaq-surge-after-nvidia-reinsta
 tes-jensen-huang-182039397.html\nIBTimes: S&P 500 surges nearly 5% as Nvid
 ia brings back Huang: https://www.ibtimes.com.au/sp-500-surges-nvidia-rein
 states-jensen-huang-ceo-1879244
CATEGORIES:stocks
URL:https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/live/stock-market-today-monday-novemb
 er-23-dow-sp-500-nasdaq-surge-after-nvidia-reinstates-jensen-huang-1820393
 97.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:53be903d3e2dba69@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART:20261125T133000Z
DTEND:20261125T143000Z
SUMMARY:US PCE inflation (October)
DESCRIPTION:The Fed's preferred inflation gauge for October\, the last infl
 ation print before the December FOMC.\n\nOctober CPI was hot at +0.4% head
 line and +0.3% core\, so a firm core PCE is the base case. A hot print rai
 ses the odds of a 50bp December hike\, which would hit crypto\, tech and g
 old. A soft print would ease hike pricing. The date comes from third-party
  calendars\, so check it against the BEA schedule. Fedratecalc lists the Q
 3 GDP second estimate for the same 8:30am ET slot. Financecalendar and For
 exfundamentals also list November 25 at 8:30am ET. No consensus figure tur
 ned up in search by November 24. It lands two days after the S&P 500 rose 
 4.7% on Huang's return to Nvidia\, with CME odds of a 50bp December hike d
 own to 0% (Bloomingbit)\, so a hot core has room to reprice. US markets ar
 e closed the next day for Thanksgiving. On the morning of the release the 
 Bloomberg consensus was core PCE +0.3% month over month and 3.2% year over
  year\, up from 3.1%\, and headline +0.3% and 3.8%\, up from 3.6%. Goldman
  Sachs estimated core at +0.29%. CME odds of a 50bp December hike were bac
 k at 4.9%. Outcome: the figures weren't found in search by November 26. Th
 e S&P 500 fell 0.3% and the Nasdaq 100 0.6% on the day of the release.\n\n
 BEA: PCE price index: https://www.bea.gov/data/personal-consumption-expend
 itures-price-index\nZeroHedge: key events this holiday-shortened week\, al
 l about PCE: https://www.zerohedge.com/markets/key-events-holiday-shortene
 d-week-all-about-pce\nFedratecalc: US economic calendar November 2026: htt
 ps://fedratecalc.com/us-economic-calendar/november-2026/
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bea.gov/data/personal-consumption-expenditures-price-index
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ce4343876b2fdf9f@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261129
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261130
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:OPEC+ ministerial meeting\, 2027 quotas
DESCRIPTION:All 21 OPEC+ members meet\, and analysts expect them to set the
  2027 production framework.\n\nAt the November 1 virtual meeting Saudi Ara
 bia\, Russia\, Iraq\, Kuwait\, Kazakhstan\, Algeria and Oman kept December
  production at the September required level and set the next meeting for N
 ovember 29 (OPEC). World Oil reports the Middle East conflict is curbing p
 art of the group's output. WTI is down about 19% in a month\, so a cut wou
 ld be the surprise and would lift oil and energy stocks. Unchanged quotas 
 are the pattern. By November 24 WTI futures were down 23.1% in a month\, e
 ven with Iran reporting three tankers hit by mines in Hormuz (CNBC). No pr
 eview of this meeting turned up in search by November 25. Reuters reports 
 the full 21-member group meets on November 29 and is expected to decide 20
 27 quotas\, after a review of members' production capacity that sets the n
 ew baselines. One layer of cuts of about 2 million barrels a day runs to t
 he end of 2026. Rystad's Jorge Leon called this meeting the much more impo
 rtant test.\n\nOPEC: statement of November 1\, 2026: https://www.opec.org/
 pr-detail/2033620-1-november-2026.html\nEngineering News (Reuters): OPEC+ 
 keeps December targets steady ahead of tougher call for 2027: https://engi
 neeringnews.co.za/article/opec-keeps-december-oil-output-targets-steady-ah
 ead-of-tougher-call-for-2027-2026-11-02\nWorld Oil: OPEC+ subgroup keeps q
 uotas unchanged for December: https://worldoil.com/news/2026/11/1/opec-sub
 group-keeps-oil-production-quotas-unchanged-for-december/
CATEGORIES:politics
URL:https://www.opec.org/pr-detail/2033620-1-november-2026.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4d7f7a7d912747d0@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:MSCI drops Strategy and Metaplanet
DESCRIPTION:Strategy leaves the MSCI USA\, World and ACWI indexes and Metap
 lanet leaves MSCI Japan Small Cap after the close.\n\nThis is the first cu
 t under MSCI's new rule for non-operating companies\, announced in the Nov
 ember review. Passive funds tracking MSCI own nearly $3bn of MSTR\, and St
 rategy itself estimates $2.8bn of its shares will be sold (Investing.com).
  JPMorgan estimated up to $8.8bn of outflows if other index providers foll
 ow. Removal doesn't force Strategy to sell bitcoin. Expect index selling i
 nto the close\, with room for a relief bounce after. By the November 23 cl
 ose the shares were down 42.2% in a month\, and by the November 24 close 4
 6.9%\, with bitcoin under $60\,000. On November 25 they rose 3.1%\, leavin
 g them down 42.8% in a month.\n\nThe Block: Strategy\, Metaplanet lose MSC
 I index membership: https://www.theblock.co/news/markets/2026-11-11-strate
 gy-metaplanet-lose-msci-index-membership-november-reshuffle-438437\nInvest
 ing.com: Strategy to be removed from MSCI indexes: https://investing.com/n
 ews/stock-market-news/strategy-to-be-removed-from-msci-indexes-what-are-th
 e-risks-for-bitcoin-93CH-5020460\nMLQ: MSCI to drop Strategy and Metaplane
 t after Nov. 30: https://mlq.ai/news/msci-confirms-it-will-drop-strategy-a
 nd-metaplanet-from-its-indexes-after-nov-30/
CATEGORIES:stocks
URL:https://www.theblock.co/news/markets/2026-11-11-strategy-metaplanet-los
 e-msci-index-membership-november-reshuffle-438437
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7836f48f0d47799b@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART:20261201T100000Z
DTEND:20261201T110000Z
SUMMARY:Eurozone flash inflation (November)
DESCRIPTION:Eurostat's flash HICP for November\, the last eurozone inflatio
 n print before the December 17 ECB decision.\n\nThird-party calendars list
  11:00 CET on December 1. One Eurostat-based schedule shows a different da
 te\, so check Eurostat's release calendar. A hot print would firm up ECB h
 awkishness while the Fed hikes\, which supports the euro and EUR/CHF. A so
 ft print widens the US-EU rate gap and favours the dollar.\n\nEurostat: re
 lease calendar: https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/news/release-calendar\nForex
 fundamentals: euro area HICP 2026-12-01: https://forexfundamentals.com/eco
 nomic-calendar/eur-cpi/2026-12-01
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/news/release-calendar
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f0f7d84bd600c7e9@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART:20261202T073000Z
DTEND:20261202T083000Z
SUMMARY:Swiss CPI (November)
DESCRIPTION:Swiss consumer prices for November\, the last print before the 
 December 10 SNB decision.\n\nThe FSO publishes at 08:30 Swiss time\, and t
 he date comes from a third-party calendar. October inflation surprised hig
 her\, though core gave some relief (investingLive). A firm print feeds tal
 k of an SNB move off 0% and supports the CHF. A soft print keeps the SNB o
 n hold and leaves intervention talk in play.\n\nFSO: consumer price index:
  https://www.bfs.admin.ch/bfs/en/home/statistics/prices/consumer-price-ind
 ex.html\nForexfundamentals: Swiss CPI 2026-12-02: https://forexfundamental
 s.com/economic-calendar/ch-cpi/2026-12-02\ninvestingLive: Swiss inflation 
 surprises higher in October: https://investinglive.com/news/swiss-inflatio
 n-surprises-higher-in-october-but-core-prices-offer-some-relief/
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bfs.admin.ch/bfs/en/home/statistics/prices/consumer-price-i
 ndex.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f4ef0bff80d9b263@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261203
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261204
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:Jensen Huang testifies before Senate committee
DESCRIPTION:Nvidia's CEO answers a Senate committee in a livestreamed heari
 ng on the Megaspeed chip export case.\n\nIt's Huang's first public testimo
 ny since he resigned on November 11 and was reinstated on November 23. Nvi
 dia rose 31.5% on his return and fell 5.9% the next day\, when Attorney Ge
 neral Blanche declined to say whether the Justice Department or FBI had in
 vestigated him. The Justice Department is running a criminal inquiry into 
 Megaspeed and the SEC is probing Nvidia's disclosures (CNBC). Damaging tes
 timony would hit Nvidia\, semis and the Nasdaq\, with crypto stocks likely
  following. A clean hearing removes one overhang. The start time wasn't fo
 und in search. On November 25 S&P warned Nvidia's credit rating could be c
 ut over rising management and governance risk (CNBC)\, after Moody's cut i
 ts outlook to stable on November 18. The shares fell 3.9% that day and wer
 e down 30.9% in a month.\n\nCNBC: Jensen Huang's and Nvidia's legal exposu
 re balloons: https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/19/nvidia-jensen-huang-legal.htm
 l\nBreitbart (AFP): Huang's return fails to dispel doubts as Nvidia shares
  drop: https://www.breitbart.com/news/huangs-return-fails-to-dispel-doubts
 -as-nvidia-shares-drop/\ninvestingLive: Moody's cuts Nvidia outlook to sta
 ble: https://investinglive.com/stocks/moody-s-cuts-nvidia-outlook-to-stabl
 e-saying-huang-s-exit-clouds-strategy-and-policy/
CATEGORIES:stocks
URL:https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/19/nvidia-jensen-huang-legal.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e1218ed29ec170db@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART:20261204T133000Z
DTEND:20261204T143000Z
SUMMARY:US jobs report (November)
DESCRIPTION:November nonfarm payrolls\, the last labour print before the De
 cember FOMC.\n\nOctober payrolls were 165k against a 65k estimate (LSEG po
 ll). Another strong print would firm up a December hike and raise the odds
  of 50bp\, which is bearish for crypto and tech. A weak print would trim h
 ike pricing and support risk assets and gold.\n\nBLS Employment Situation 
 schedule: https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/empsit.htm
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/empsit.htm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2629ea169b240101@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART:20261209T190000Z
DTEND:20261209T200000Z
SUMMARY:FOMC rate decision
DESCRIPTION:A 25bp hike from 3.75–4.00% is the market's base case after t
 he hot October CPI.\n\nThe Fed held at its October 28 meeting\, with Cook 
 and Hammack dissenting for a 25bp hike (Newsquawk). Before CPI\, Kalshi pr
 iced a 25bp hike at 77%. After CPI\, CME FedWatch priced 88.8% for 25bp\, 
 and the rest of the odds sat on 50bp. By November 12 the 50bp odds were 13
 .2% (Stocktwits). Newsquawk put money-market odds of 50bp at about 10% aft
 er CPI\, with 25bp fully priced. Waller had said 50bp should be considered
  if core CPI came in at 0.3% or higher\, and it did. Logan said it may be 
 possible to move more rapidly\, and Goolsbee called the inflation outlook 
 borderline disturbing. A 50bp hike or hawkish guidance would hit crypto\, 
 tech and gold. A hold would set off a relief rally. After the S&P 500 fell
  into correction on November 20\, CME odds of 50bp dropped to 0% by Novemb
 er 23 (Bloomingbit)\, and sources put 25bp between 88.6% and 95%. Governor
  Cook said waiting risks falling behind the curve and hinted at hikes beyo
 nd December\, while Bessent and Ackman warned of a policy error. By Novemb
 er 24 CME FedWatch had 25bp at about 95.1% and 50bp at about 4.9%. New Yor
 k Fed President Williams said inflation is simply too high and left hikes 
 at back-to-back meetings open. Yardeni argued for 50bp (Stocktwits). Oxfor
 d Economics expects 25bp and said in a November 16 note that markets overp
 rice 50bp. No FedWatch reading after the November 25 PCE release was found
  in search by November 26.\n\nKalshi Fed rate odds: https://kalshi.com/fed
 -rate-odds\nInvesting.com: Fed hike odds at 88% after hot CPI: https://www
 .investing.com/news/economy-news/fed-rate-hike-odds-in-december-at-88-afte
 r-hot-cpi-cme-fedwatch-5017585\nBloomingbit: 50bp December hike odds drop 
 to zero: https://en.bloomingbit.io/feed/news/125006
CATEGORIES:central bank
URL:https://kalshi.com/fed-rate-odds
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:76eb64214b7d8db5@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART:20261210T083000Z
DTEND:20261210T093000Z
SUMMARY:SNB monetary policy assessment
DESCRIPTION:Quarterly SNB decision\, with the policy rate at 0%.\n\nThe pol
 icy rate has been 0% since June 2025 (financecalendar). In March\, Continu
 um Economics judged market pricing of a possible December 2026 hike overdo
 ne\, and that view may be stale. Watch the wording on CHF strength and FX 
 intervention. A dovish tone or intervention talk weakens the CHF\, and a h
 ike would strengthen it and weigh on Swiss exporters. Switzerland is among
  the 16 partners in the US Section 301 tariff plan reported on November 24
 . The US announced new tariffs on November 25 (BBC)\, and the rates weren'
 t found in search. The franc gained in the week to November 26\, with USD/
 CHF down 1.3% and EUR/CHF down 1.4%.\n\nSNB media events schedule: https:/
 /www.snb.ch/en/ifor/media/id/media_events\nFinancecalendar: SNB rate decis
 ion December 2026: https://www.financecalendar.com/event/snb-rate-decision
 -december-2026/
CATEGORIES:central bank
URL:https://www.snb.ch/en/ifor/media/id/media_events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8c55e640f5a908f7@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART:20261210T133000Z
DTEND:20261210T143000Z
SUMMARY:US CPI (November)
DESCRIPTION:November consumer prices\, released the day after the FOMC deci
 sion.\n\nOctober came in hot at +0.4% headline and +0.3% core. Because it 
 lands right after the Fed\, a hot print would test whatever guidance the F
 ed gave and could revive 2027 hike pricing\, which is bearish for crypto a
 nd tech. A soft print would support risk assets.\n\nBLS CPI release schedu
 le: https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/cpi.htm
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/cpi.htm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1435df0c22a5f853@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261214
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:G20 leaders' summit\, Miami
DESCRIPTION:The US hosts the G20\, where SCMP expects the main US-China del
 iverables after APEC.\n\nXi told Trump the two would meet at APEC and then
  at the G20 (theworlddata\, unconfirmed by an official source). Trump's AP
 EC attendance was earlier reported to depend partly on Xi agreeing to come
  to the G20. It lands between the FOMC and the ECB\, BoE and BoJ decisions
 . A trade deal would lift Chinese stocks\, the Nasdaq and crypto\, and a b
 reakdown would hit them. The US-China trade truce runs to January 10 (TNW)
 \, which makes this the last leaders' meeting before it lapses. The Shenzh
 en meeting on November 19 did little on trade (Modern Ghana)\, which leave
 s the truce extension to this summit. On November 24 reports said the US i
 s preparing Section 301 tariffs on 16 partners including China\, which the
  BBC says is likely to raise tensions before the summit. The tariffs were 
 announced on November 25. China denounced them as baseless and Brazil call
 ed them unacceptable (Guardian).\n\nSCMP: Xi and Trump set APEC talks\, de
 liverables wait for G20: https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article
 /3373969/xi-and-trump-set-apec-talks-major-deliverables-expected-wait-g20\
 nTheworlddata: APEC summit: https://theworlddata.com/apec-summit/
CATEGORIES:politics
URL:https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3373969/xi-and-trump-
 set-apec-talks-major-deliverables-expected-wait-g20
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:59bfc848f5c9b78e@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261218
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:ECB rate decision
DESCRIPTION:The last ECB decision of 2026\, with new staff projections that
  set the starting point for 2027.\n\nFinancecalendar and Admiral Markets b
 oth list December 17. Sources disagree on the exact time\, and the ECB's o
 wn calendar should confirm it. The projections matter more than the rate. 
 A hawkish turn while the Fed is hiking would support the euro and weigh on
  the CHF cross. A dovish one would widen the US-EU rate gap.\n\nFinancecal
 endar: ECB rate decision December 2026: https://www.financecalendar.com/ev
 ent/ecb-rate-decision-december-2026/\nAdmiral Markets: ECB meeting dates 2
 026: https://admiralmarkets.com/analytics/traders-blog/ecb-meeting-october
 -2026
CATEGORIES:central bank
URL:https://www.financecalendar.com/event/ecb-rate-decision-december-2026/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:db3e3586be695d54@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261219
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:Bank of Japan rate decision
DESCRIPTION:A hike from 1.25% to 1.5% is the consensus at the December 17-1
 8 meeting.\n\nThe BoJ held at 1.25% on October 30 by an 8-1 vote\, with Ta
 kata voting for 1.5%. A Bloomberg survey has 83% of economists expecting a
  December hike\, up from 35% a month earlier. Daiwa and MUFG both forecast
  December and then April 2027. A hike strengthens the yen and can force ca
 rry trades to unwind\, which hit crypto and tech in past hikes. A hold wou
 ld weaken the yen. On November 16 CNBC reported Japan's economy unexpected
 ly contracted in the third quarter on energy costs\, which cuts against th
 e hike consensus.\n\ninvestingLive: Daiwa sees December BoJ hike: https://
 investinglive.com/central-banks/daiwa-sees-next-boj-rate-hike-in-december-
 as-ueda-signals-shift-in-policy-phase/\ninvestingLive: Bloomberg survey\, 
 most see December hike: https://investinglive.com/central-banks/most-analy
 sts-now-expect-the-next-boj-rate-hike-in-december-none-see-october-move-bl
 oomberg/\nFinancecalendar: BoJ rate decision December 2026: https://www.fi
 nancecalendar.com/?p=1260
CATEGORIES:central bank
URL:https://investinglive.com/central-banks/daiwa-sees-next-boj-rate-hike-i
 n-december-as-ueda-signals-shift-in-policy-phase/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5e5318a9d3229b75@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART:20270108T133000Z
DTEND:20270108T143000Z
SUMMARY:US jobs report (December)
DESCRIPTION:December nonfarm payrolls\, the first labour print after the De
 cember FOMC.\n\nThe BLS 2027 schedule lists January 8 at 8:30am ET. Octobe
 r payrolls were 165k against a 65k estimate (LSEG poll). A strong print wo
 uld keep 2027 hikes in play ahead of the January 27 FOMC\, which is bearis
 h for crypto and tech. A weak one would support risk assets and gold.\n\nB
 LS: 2027 release schedule: https://www.bls.gov/schedule/2027/home.htm
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bls.gov/schedule/2027/home.htm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bff26671e0d1417f@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270111
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:US-China trade truce expires
DESCRIPTION:The US-China tariff truce runs out unless it's extended again.\
 n\nTNW reported the truce was extended to January 10 at the end of Xi's Wa
 shington visit\, when the two sides also set up an AI dialogue and left ra
 re earths and chip rules for further talks. The date isn't confirmed by an
  official source yet. Ahead of APEC both governments extended their suspen
 sions of trade measures and port fees (SCMP). SCMP expects the main US-Chi
 na deliverables at the G20 on December 14\, so an extension could come the
 re. A lapse would bring tariffs back and hit the Nasdaq\, the Hang Seng an
 d crypto. An extension or a wider deal would lift them. Cyprus Mail also g
 ives January 10\, 2027 as the end of a two-month extension\, and reports T
 rump revived threats of tariffs of up to 300% on countries that don't shif
 t production to the US. The Shenzhen meeting on November 19 brought no ext
 ension (Modern Ghana). On November 24 reports said the US is preparing Sec
 tion 301 tariffs on 16 partners\, with China likely facing some of the ste
 epest increases (Axios\, Fiscal Times). The US announced the tariffs on No
 vember 25\, and China called the levies baseless (BBC\, Guardian).\n\nTNW:
  Xi ends Washington visit with trade truce extended to January: https://th
 enextweb.com/news/xi-washington-visit-trade-truce-ai-talks\nCyprus Mail: T
 rump-Xi meeting just kicked the can down the road: https://cyprus-mail.com
 /2026/10/18/trump-xi-meeting-just-kicked-can-down-the-road\nSCMP: Xi and T
 rump's APEC meeting\, what's on hold and what's on the table: https://www.
 scmp.com/economy/china-economy/article/3373904/xi-and-trumps-apec-meeting-
 whats-hold-and-whats-table
CATEGORIES:politics
URL:https://thenextweb.com/news/xi-washington-visit-trade-truce-ai-talks
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:58b4477072f2044d@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART:20270113T133000Z
DTEND:20270113T143000Z
SUMMARY:US CPI (December)
DESCRIPTION:December consumer prices\, the last CPI print before the Januar
 y 27 FOMC.\n\nThe BLS 2027 schedule lists January 13 at 8:30am ET. October
  came in hot at +0.4% headline and +0.3% core. A hot print would raise the
  odds of another hike in January\, which hurts crypto\, tech and gold. A s
 oft print would support the case that December was the last move.\n\nBLS: 
 2027 release schedule: https://www.bls.gov/schedule/2027/home.htm
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bls.gov/schedule/2027/home.htm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:926b93dfd5a1b792@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T054758Z
DTSTART:20270127T190000Z
DTEND:20270127T200000Z
SUMMARY:FOMC rate decision
DESCRIPTION:The first Fed decision of 2027\, after the January 26-27 meetin
 g.\n\nThe Fed set the date in its tentative 2027 schedule. Williams said i
 n October he saw no case for 2027 hikes (investingLive)\, so guidance here
  shows whether December was the last move. A hawkish surprise would hit cr
 ypto and tech. In November Governor Cook hinted at hikes beyond December (
 KuCoin news). On November 23 Williams said inflation is simply too high an
 d left hikes at back-to-back meetings open.\n\nFederal Reserve: tentative 
 2027 FOMC schedule: https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressrelease
 s/monetary20250905a.htm\nThrive in Markets: FOMC 2027 dates: https://thriv
 einmarkets.com/calendar/dates/fomc-2027/\nKuCoin news: Cook hints at rate 
 hikes beyond December: https://www.kucoin.com/news/flash/fed-governor-lisa
 -cook-hints-at-rate-hikes-beyond-december
CATEGORIES:central bank
URL:https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary2025090
 5a.htm
END:VEVENT
